Say which descriptors are still armed when a kevent is about to wait with no timeout.

A wait with a NULL timeout means the caller believes it has work outstanding, and nothing said
which descriptors it was still watching. A handle nobody closes and an event nobody sends look
identical from outside, and that is exactly the state CMake ends in.

Under the existing KQUEUE_DEBUG switch, every untimed wait is now preceded by one line per live
knote:

  knote_dump_armed(): still armed: filter=-1 ident=18 flags=0x1 fflags=0x0 dupfd=21

The walk lives in knote.c rather than kevent.c because the red-black accessors are generated
there; kevent.c calls it through one extern.

WHAT IT SHOWED (#235): after CMake reaps its child, the kqueue is still armed on three EVFILT_READ
descriptors and nothing else. Reading the hung process fd table from inside the container, where
the guest is root, those descriptors are pipe read ends whose WRITE ends are still open in the
same process, so they can never report end of file and the wait can never end.

--- a/src/common/kevent.c
+++ b/src/common/kevent.c
@@ -326,6 +326,7 @@
 }
 
 extern pthread_mutex_t kq_mtx;
+extern void knote_dump_armed(struct kqueue *);
 
 int VISIBLE
 kevent64_impl(int kqfd, const struct kevent64_s *changelist, int nchanges,
@@ -397,6 +398,8 @@
         /* WHAT IS THIS LOOP STILL WAITING FOR. A wait with no timeout means the caller believes it
          * has work outstanding, and until now nothing said which descriptors were still armed: a
          * handle nobody closes and an event nobody sends look identical from outside. Task #235. */
+        if (DEBUG_KQUEUE && ts == NULL)
+            knote_dump_armed(kq);
         rv = kqops.kevent_wait(kq, nevents, ts);
         dbg_printf("kqops.kevent_wait returned %d", rv);
 
--- a/src/common/knote.c
+++ b/src/common/knote.c
@@ -79,6 +79,25 @@
     pthread_rwlock_unlock(&filt->kf_knote_mtx);
 }
 
+/* WHAT IS THIS KQUEUE STILL WAITING FOR. A wait with no timeout means the caller believes it has
+ * work outstanding, and nothing said which descriptors were still armed: a handle nobody closes
+ * and an event nobody sends look identical from outside. Task #235. */
+void
+knote_dump_armed(struct kqueue *kq)
+{
+    for (int f = 0; f < EVFILT_SYSCOUNT; f++) {
+        struct filter *filt = &kq->kq_filt[f];
+        struct knote *kn;
+
+        if (filt->kf_id == 0)
+            continue;
+        RB_FOREACH(kn, knt, &filt->kf_knote)
+            dbg_printf("still armed: filter=%d ident=%d flags=0x%x fflags=0x%x dupfd=%d",
+                    (int) kn->kev.filter, (int) kn->kev.ident, (unsigned) kn->kev.flags,
+                    (unsigned) kn->kev.fflags, (int) kn->kdata.kn_dupfd);
+    }
+}
+
 int
 knote_delete(struct filter *filt, struct knote *kn)
